      "text": "Since $x$ is a multiple of $15336$, we have $x=15336n$ for some non-negative integer $n$.\n\nNote that $x+1$, $x+3$, $x+4$, and $x+5$ are all multiples of $3$, $7$, $11$, and $13$, respectively.  Therefore, $f(x)$ is divisible by $3\\cdot 7\\cdot 11\\cdot 13 = 2772$.\n\nSince $x$ is also a multiple of $15336$, we therefore have $x \\equiv 0 \\pmod{15336}$. Finally, $f(x) \\equiv f(0) \\equiv 0^{15336} \\cdot 4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 6 \\cdot 9\\equiv 0 \\pmod{2772}$. Thus,\n\\[\\gcd(f(x), x) \\boxed{2772}.\\]The answer is: 2772",
