      "text": "To find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of \\( f(x) = (3x+4)(7x+1)(13x+6)(2x+9) \\) and \\( x \\), we need to analyze how the terms in \\( f(x) \\) change when \\( x \\) is divisible by 15336. Since \\( x \\) is a multiple of 15336, we can write \\( x = 15336k \\) for some integer \\( k \\).\n\nFirst, consider each factor in \\( f(x) \\):\n1. \\( 3x + 4 = 15336k \\cdot 3 + 4 = 45996k + 4 \\)\n2. \\( 7x + 1 = 15336k \\cdot 7 + 1 = 107352k + 1 \\)\n3. \\( 13x + 6 = 15336k \\cdot 13 + 6 = 199368k + 6 \\)\n4. \\( 2x + 9 = 15336k \\cdot 2 + 9 = 30672k + 9 \\)\n\nThe GCD of \\( 15336k \\), \\( 45996k + 4 \\), \\( 107352k + 1 \\), \\( 199368k + 6 \\), and \\( 30672k + 9 \\) depends on the GCD of the constant terms and the coefficients modulo M.\n\nFor any multiple of 15336, each of these expressions will satisfy:\n\\[ \\gcd(45996k + 4, 107352k + 1, 199368k + 6, 30672k + 9) \\]\n\nSince the coefficients are all multiples of 15336, the GCD of the constant terms 4, 1, 6, and 9 will be 1. Thus, the GCD of the entire expression will also be:\n\\[ \\gcd(45996k + 4, 107352k + 1, 199368k + 6, 30672k + 9) = 1 \\]\n\nTherefore, the greatest common divisor of \\( f(x) \\) and \\( x \\) is \\( \\boxed{1} \\).",
